+  accepted forms MUST be validated by a default-deny allow-list (an unlisted flag
+  is refused), and an operator-supplied project `Approve`/`Deny` policy MUST be
+  honored when present (it can only tighten). No project configuration currently
+  supplies an `Approve`/`Deny` policy for acceptance checks, so it MUST NOT be
+  described as enforced today.
+- Confining a cargo check's `--manifest-path` to the repository root limits which
+  manifest file is named. It MUST NOT be described as a sandbox: the crate's build
+  scripts, proc-macros, tests, and dependency downloads are unaffected.
 
